## Follow through on actionable findings

- Treat a request to investigate or fix an issue as authorization to do the related work.
- When you identify a necessary next step, do it before ending the turn.
- Do not stop at saying what you should have inspected or offering to continue.
- Stop only for missing evidence, a real blocker, or an action that needs user approval.
- State the exact blocker and complete all independent work first.
- Preserve the agreed UI during protocol and bug fixes unless the user requests a layout change.
- Trace the complete source path before changing reverse-engineered behavior.
- Separate source evidence, automated tests, and physical verification.
